gar4(){return"Open Settings, choose Change email, and enter your new address below Current email. Select Send confirmation email and open the link sent to your new inbox. The screen distinguishes the New email to confirm from the address you should still use to sign in. Once complete, the status becomes Email updated: use the new address next time you sign in and press Back to settings. When you open this screen or return to the app, an online check reads the current address and any pending request: this check does not send an email or change your account."},
gar5(){return"If the email does not arrive, check your spam folder. In a pending request, Check status verifies the outcome without sending another email; Resend requests another confirmation and Correct address reopens the form. Back to pending request only closes correction. Cancel request is separate at the bottom and requires confirmation. Additional guidance is under How it works. If the status is uncertain, check it again before making further changes. In the confirmation dialog, Go back keeps the request; Cancel request cancels it."},
gatT(){return"How do I leave a project?"},
garG(){return"Open the project selector in the calendar, choose Leave project, and confirm. You will leave all its groups and lose access to the project calendar. Shared events stay in the project and your personal unavailability stays in your calendar. You will need a new invitation to rejoin."},
garH(){return"If you own the project, first transfer ownership to another member in the project settings. Then return to the selector and confirm that you want to leave."},
gauM(){return"Find a date and polls"},
gatM(){return"How do I compare availability and propose dates to the band?"},
garu(){return"If you have the Admin or Normal role, switch to Band mode, tap +, and choose Find a date. Select the musicians and the date range, then choose Compare dates. From the results, you can use a date to create an event right away or choose Propose to the band, select 2 to 5 dates, review the recipients, and send the poll."},
gatC(){return"Where do I find a poll and how do I vote?"},
gari(){return"In the project calendar, open the project selector and choose Open polls. A dot next to the project name indicates open polls available to you. If you are a recipient, you can vote on each date even if you have the Limited role. For each remaining date, choose I can make it, Maybe, or I can\u2019t make it. You can change your vote while the poll is open and the date has not passed."},
gatB(){return"How do I review responses and choose the final date?"},
garg(){return"The poll organizer and project owner can see the summary and each musician\u2019s responses if they have permission to create events. They can send one reminder per poll per day to musicians who still have a remaining date to vote on and have push notifications enabled."},
garh(){return"Choose Use this date to open the editor. You can save a rehearsal or a live event. The poll closes when you save the event. Proposed dates do not mark you as busy in the calendar."},
gauJ(){return"Offline calendar on Android"},
gatl(){return"What can I see in the Android calendar without a connection?"},
gaqV(){return"After loading a project online in the Android app, you can view rehearsals and live events you have access to for up to 90 days ahead, within the range shown in the banner. In Personal mode, you can also see your saved unavailability without private notes. If you have several saved projects, you can switch between them."},
gaqW(){return"The saved copy is available for 48 hours after the last successful load. Go online to view dates outside the downloaded range or save changes."},
gauf(){return"How do I change my profile photo or avatar?"},
gasn(){return"Open Settings, then Personal details and Choose avatar. You can upload a Personal photo, pick an icon from the Music catalog, or remove your avatar to show your initials. Press Use this avatar and then Save changes on the Personal details screen. Closing the picker without pressing Use this avatar discards your selection. Your account menu avatar shows the same saved photo or icon, or your initials; it updates after saving."},
gauv(){return"How do I remove someone from just one group?"},
gasQ(){return"If you own the project, open its settings, select the group, and choose Remove member from the person\u2019s menu. Confirm and save the project. The person remains in any other groups they belong to. Removing them from their last group also removes their access to the project."},
gaui(){return"What happens if the owner is inactive or the project is archived?"},
gass(){return"If the ownership process starts because the owner is inactive, eligible Admins are offered ownership first. If none accepts, the offer can go to other eligible members. If you receive an offer, open Review proposal from the calendar and accept or decline by the deadline. Declining leaves your role as it was."},
gast(){return"If nobody accepts by the final deadline, the project is archived. You can still view events in read-only mode according to your permissions. If you\u2019re eligible to reactivate the project, the archive screen offers Take ownership and reactivate."},
gatr(){return"How do I see the month\u2019s appointments in a list?"},
gar2(){return"Select Switch to list view next to the month name. The list follows the current Personal or Band mode and your permissions. Choose Switch to calendar view to return to the grid."},
gatI(){return"How do I add a venue to a rehearsal or live event?"},
garp(){return"In the event editor, under Place, choose Search for a place and select the address or venue from the results. If the search does not respond, check your connection and tap Retry. If you have made too many searches, wait before trying again. You can also use Choose city only when place search is unavailable. When an exact location is available, Directions in the event details opens Google Maps. City search shows up to 8 results. If the list is limited, type more letters to narrow your search."},
gatG(){return"How do I duplicate a rehearsal, including a past one?"},
garm(){return"If you can create events in the project, open the original rehearsal and choose Duplicate rehearsal. Select a new date from today onward. The draft copies the original description, city, and venue and starts as To be confirmed."},
garn(){return"Saving creates a new rehearsal and leaves the original intact. Participation and sharing with Limited members are managed for the new rehearsal."},
gatq(){return"How do I add a live event or rehearsal to my own calendar?"},
gar1(){return"Open the live event or rehearsal and choose Add to calendar. On Android, this opens your device\u2019s calendar editor. On the web, choose Google Calendar, Outlook, or Download .ics. The appointment is exported as an all-day event. Later changes in Band Calendar won\u2019t update the external calendar."},
gatJ(){return"How do I share a rehearsal or live event?"},
garq(){return"Open the event details and choose Share event. In the preview, choose Copy text or choose Share to open your device\u2019s share menu when available. The text includes the event details and a directions link if a location was added. Private notes are excluded."},
