gal4(){return"Appointments with more than one band on the same day. Check the times before confirming new commitments."},
gauc(){return"Where can I see appointments from all my bands together?"},
gash(){return"Open Agenda from the bottom bar. It shows rehearsals and live events visible to you in active projects, initially from today through the next 12 months, with each band name. Search by title, place or band; searching also loads subsequent pages. Period lets you choose 30 days, 12 months or specific future dates. The search icon at the top opens Search events for the filtered project, or the project selected in Calendar, including past events. Pull down the list to refresh Agenda; a connection is required. The search icon at the top of Today and Calendar opens the Search events screen for the selected project, with date and history search. Agenda remains available from the bottom bar with its own search field across bands."},
gasi(){return"In Filters, choose a band, event type and whether to include your personal unavailability or declined events. Show results applies your changes; Close discards them. Reset restores the draft choices, which still need Show results to apply. Remove active filters using their chips. Personal unavailability stays visible when filtering by band or type; private notes stay yours. Project permissions also apply in Agenda. The expandable warning means multiple bands have events on the same day, not necessarily overlapping times. Open an event and choose Show in calendar to reach its project and day. After Opt out, the details stay open so you can choose Rejoin or use the other actions. When you close them, the list follows your declined-event filter."},
